==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AuthRequiredEverywhere  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AuthRequiredEverywhere.als
    rationale: Removing this fact lets the model invent a successful operation with no authenticated caller, directly violating the FR-001/SC-005 'authentication required everywhere' invariant.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired, FR_004_FlatPermissions
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_FlatPermissions: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyDeletionLog  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyDeletionLog.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the one-to-one binding between TaskDeletion atoms and their creating DeleteOp; the injection forces an orphan log entry with no creating operation, which is exactly the mutation/insertion the append-only contract forbids.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DeleteLogCompleteness  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_DeleteLogCompleteness.als
    rationale: Without completeness, the model can produce a successful DeleteOp that leaves no operational-log entry, which is exactly the FR-018 violation auditors must detect.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_012_PermanentDelete
      - AuditCompleteness: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_012_PermanentDelete: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_DeletionAttribution  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_DeletionAttribution.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact lets the deletion log record someone other than the actual caller, which is the canonical attribution-correctness violation.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_018_DeletionLog
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_DeletionLog: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ClosedTaskRule  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_ClosedTaskRule.als
    rationale: Without this rule the model can succeed on an edit of a done task that does not reopen it, which is precisely the contract violation FR-011 forbids and the 409 task_closed response is designed to surface.
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_ClosedTaskRule
      - FR_011_ClosedTaskRule: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_TitleValid  → runs/B-L1/mutated_F_TitleValid.als
    rationale: Clearing the title-validation invariant lets a Task exist with an invalid (empty or too-long) title; this is the validation-before-mutation contract failure for FR-005.
    expected to FAIL: ValidationBeforeMutation, FR_005_TitleValid, FR_006_DescriptionBounds
      - ValidationBeforeMutation: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_005_TitleValid: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_DescriptionBounds: FAIL (expected)

